{
  "sticker": "flower",
  "skeleton": "flower facing the viewer: root at the stem's foot (in the ground); stem bone(s) up the stem so it can sway and droop; head (petals and disc) at the top of the stem, face on the disc with eyes and mouth; a closed-bud piece swaps in for the head; leafL/leafR on the stem (wave).",
  "sheets": [
    {
      "id": "parts",
      "size": "1536x1024",
      "prompt": "Image 1 is a sticker of a smiling flower character. Draw this exact flower as a cut-out paper puppet: its separate body parts laid out on one sheet, the same drawing style, colours, texture, line and proportions as in image 1, every part at the size it has in image 1.\n\nDraw each part on its own, spread out over the sheet with wide empty gaps between them, no part touching or overlapping another:\n1. the flower head: the round flower with its ring of yellow petals and brown seed disc, facing the viewer as in image 1, with a completely blank face on the disc — no eyes, no mouth — keep the rosy cheeks; without the stem.\n2. the closed flower: the same flower closed for the night, its yellow petals folded up together over its face like a bud.\n3. the stem: the green stem alone, without leaves, both ends rounded.\n4. one leaf: the leaf on the right of image 1, with a rounded base.\n\nEvery part is drawn whole, including what is normally hidden behind another part, and each joint end (where it tucks under the body or the head) is a full, smooth, rounded edge. No text, no labels, no numbers, no outline around the parts beyond the drawing's own line, no shadows. Fully transparent background."
    },
    {
      "id": "face",
      "size": "1536x1024",
      "references": [
        "parts"
      ],
      "prompt": "Image 1 is a sticker of a smiling flower character; image 2 shows the same flower cut into puppet parts, with a blank face. Draw the flower's face pieces as separate stickers on one sheet: the same drawing style, colours and line as in image 1, every piece at the size it has on the flower in image 1, so it fits the blank face in image 2.\n\nDraw each piece on its own, spread out in tidy rows with wide empty gaps between them, nothing touching:\n1. the flower's left eye (on the right of image 1) as it is in image 1: a dark round eye with a white sparkle.\n2. the same eye wide open and surprised: bigger and rounder, with its white sparkle.\n3. the same eye gently closed in sleep: a soft downward-curving line with a few lashes.\n4. the same eye closed in a happy smile: an upward-curving arc.\n5. the same eye sad: looking down, its upper lid tilted up towards the middle.\n6. the mouth as it is in image 1: a small happy smile.\n7. the mouth wide open in a big happy laugh, the inside pink.\n8. the mouth open in a small round 'o'.\n9. the mouth in a small sad frown.\n\nNo text, no labels, no numbers, no shadows, no face or head around the pieces. Fully transparent background."
    }
  ],
